steps.message:
The analysis has been completed. The DC-OPF model with reserve co-optimization was implemented and executed for both the base case and the counterfactual scenario (where the transmission line 64-1501 thermal capacity was increased by 20%).

The analysis revealed that the line connecting **Bus 64 to Bus 1501 was not binding** in the base case scenario. Consequently, relaxing this constraint had a negligible impact on the system cost and LMPs, suggesting that this line is not the cause of the congestion suspected by the system managers.

The results are saved in `report.json`.

